  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $B={n\\in Z:2n-11<-4}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $2n-11<-4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n-11 & <-4 \\\\ 2n & <7 \\\\ n & <\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $3,2,1,0,-1,-2,\u2026.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nB={\u2026,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}.\n$$",
